FEX: host memory in 32-bit guests' reach; 32-bit layout of FEX's own thunks (SteamARM, Darwin host)

Exports fex_lxrt_guest_bits/_reserve/_release to host libraries: a 32-bit
guest lives at host = base + guest, so memory a host library maps
(vkMapMemory) is out of its reach. The runtime's Vulkan shim reserves a
range in the guest allocator, aliases the host pages into the window and
returns the window address.

Also: LoadLib/IsLibLoaded read the guest thunk library's structures in the
guest's pointer size (4 bytes for i386) and through the guest base: FEX
faulted reading 0xf754a0f2 on an i386 guest's first libvulkan load (MEASURED).

